1
00:00:14,598 --> 00:00:19,937
HELLO, TWENTY - WONHEE

2
00:00:22,564 --> 00:00:24,191
Hello.

3
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:25,984
Hello.

4
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:29,446
DON'T FORGET TO CLOSE THE DOOR

5
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:30,948
Good morning.

6
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:34,618
- Can you guess what you'll be doing?
- Well...

7
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:36,578
I suppose...

8
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:37,788
A <i>mukbang </i>show?

9
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:39,122
I'm ready for that.

10
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:40,040
BAGGY SHIRT

11
00:00:40,624 --> 00:00:42,209
You're actually hitting a club.

12
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:44,336
That would be a first for me.

13
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:46,547
I'm not sure you're dressed for clubbing.

14
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:50,342
But we all know what's really going on.

15
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,177
WE'RE FIVE EPISODES IN

16
00:00:52,261 --> 00:00:54,638
As you know, we're visiting a boxing gym.

17
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:55,639
EPISODE 5: BOXING

18
00:00:58,809 --> 00:00:59,726
IS THIS A PREVIEW?

19
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,478
I know a few moves.

20
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:03,522
A MUST FOR 20-YEAR-OLDS:
BUILD A HEALTHIER LIFE

21
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:06,358
IT'S BEST TO MAKE AN EFFORT
TO MAINTAIN OVERALL WELL-BEING

22
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:09,194
WHERE IS OUR 20-YEAR-OLD VISITING
TO GET STARTED IN THIS JOURNEY?

23
00:01:09,278 --> 00:01:11,697
TODAY'S LOCATION:
BOXING GYM

24
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:13,740
Today's girlie is a big name.

25
00:01:13,824 --> 00:01:16,743
Of course, she's a star among stars.

26
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:19,162
She's got rizz from head to toe.

27
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:20,247
COME ALONG, WONHEE

28
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:22,207
I'm far from a boxer.

29
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:25,043
Here it is.

30
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:28,797
So this is it.

31
00:01:32,426 --> 00:01:36,138
Patricia.

32
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:40,684
Wonhee!

33
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:42,060
EPISODE 5 GIRLIE
PATRICIA

34
00:01:42,686 --> 00:01:44,146
- Hello.
- Hello.

35
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:45,022
BOUNCY

36
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:47,190
This is painfully awkward.

37
00:01:47,274 --> 00:01:48,400
SO AWKWARD

38
00:01:48,692 --> 00:01:50,235
How did you know?

39
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:51,737
It's so awkward.

40
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:53,822
I didn't know you trained here.

41
00:01:53,864 --> 00:01:55,365
Oh, well...

42
00:01:55,449 --> 00:01:56,366
ALMOST FELL

43
00:01:56,408 --> 00:01:57,534
Why am I already out of breath?

44
00:01:57,576 --> 00:01:58,702
LAUGHS OUT LOUD

45
00:01:58,744 --> 00:02:00,287
What brings you here?

46
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:04,625
People in their 20s are
really into wellness these days.

47
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:06,543
THAT'S TRUE
So I wanted

48
00:02:06,627 --> 00:02:08,712
to build both my body and mind.

49
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:11,298
And what better way than boxing?

50
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:12,591
How old are you exactly?

51
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:14,134
- I just turned 20.
- You're 20?

52
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:15,093
Yes.

53
00:02:15,177 --> 00:02:17,554
- Now that I'm no longer a teenager,
- Incredible.

54
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:19,389
- I feel easily drained.
- They want us over here.

55
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:21,558
I'm so sorry!

56
00:02:21,642 --> 00:02:23,727
I thought this was the center.

57
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,062
PLEASE FORGIVE ME

58
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:27,064
- So you turned 20?
- Yeah.

59
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:29,274
Gosh, you're just a baby.

60
00:02:29,358 --> 00:02:31,943
I'm 25 this year.

61
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:33,570
Come on, that's still young.

62
00:02:33,612 --> 00:02:36,031
No, I just told you I'm 25!

63
00:02:36,073 --> 00:02:38,325
What was turning 20 like for you?

64
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:40,911
I'd been waiting for that day
since I was 19.

65
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:44,081
So you were one of the cuties going,
"I'm 20 now!"

66
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:45,707
I was like, "I can't wait!"

67
00:02:45,749 --> 00:02:49,252
I was excited not to be stuck
in a uniform every day.

68
00:02:49,336 --> 00:02:52,255
I wanted the freedom to choose

69
00:02:52,756 --> 00:02:54,257
whatever I wanted to wear.

70
00:02:54,341 --> 00:02:56,593
And I couldn't wait
to be done with school.

71
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,971
Getting to school by 8:30 a.m. every day

72
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:01,890
- is pretty rough.
- It's tough.

73
00:03:01,932 --> 00:03:03,934
After I turned 20...

74
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:05,018
How do I put this?

75
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:07,396
The world felt completely different.

76
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:09,231
- Were you that excited?
- "I'm legal now.

77
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:11,608
- No one can mess with me now."
- So cute.

78
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:14,945
- "I'm legal now."
- "No one can touch me."

79
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:17,531
What was the first thing you did
once you became an adult?

80
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:19,616
What did I do first?

81
00:03:20,701 --> 00:03:22,869
I think I tried alcohol
for the first time.

82
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:25,163
I wanted to know what soju tasted like.

83
00:03:25,247 --> 00:03:26,832
Everyone makes that "ahh" sound
when they drink.

84
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:28,792
- That sparked my curiosity.
- I see.

85
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:30,794
I threw it all out after one sip.

86
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:32,129
- Me too.
- I emptied the bottle.

87
00:03:32,212 --> 00:03:35,507
Seriously, I wanted to exclaim
like everyone else.

88
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:37,676
- Just for show, you know.
- Okay.

89
00:03:39,261 --> 00:03:40,470
But I almost spat it out.

90
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:41,471
Let's go.

91
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:43,223
FIRST TASTE OF SOJU IN EPISODE 1,
GIRLIE'S NIGHT

92
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:45,350
Jeez.

93
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:48,145
BAD MEMORY
It literally tastes like an alcohol swab.

94
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:50,814
People say it's sweet,
but don't fall for that.

95
00:03:50,856 --> 00:03:51,815
It's not sweet.

96
00:03:51,857 --> 00:03:52,899
In fact, it's bitter.

97
00:03:52,983 --> 00:03:53,817
Downright awful.

98
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:55,819
We're at a boxing gym, right?

99
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:58,739
Everyone's working hard
to build a healthier life.

100
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,532
What kind of exercise are you into?

101
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:03,160
Just call me a generous donor.

102
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,995
- To your gym?
- Yes, exactly.

103
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:07,748
My brother, Jonathan,
keeps calling me a donor

104
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:09,750
like it's a compliment.

105
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,418
- Is that a compliment, though?
- Sure.

106
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:14,671
For what it's worth,
now that I'm a bit older,

107
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:18,300
I realize I need to work out
to stay in shape.

108
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:22,053
Now that my teenage days are over,
I feel the same need.

109
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:23,388
You're so...

110
00:04:23,597 --> 00:04:25,223
I mean, I'm 25.

111
00:04:25,307 --> 00:04:27,434
WHAT IS SHE SAYING?

112
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:30,687
Have you tried boxing before?

113
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,439
Actually, no.

114
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:34,232
- Is it your first time?
- Have you tried it before?

115
00:04:34,316 --> 00:04:36,193
Not at all.

116
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:39,029
- I thought you had.
- Are we both newbies?

117
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:40,989
At least one of us

118
00:04:41,031 --> 00:04:43,450
- should know how it goes.
- Wait.

119
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:44,910
- You had the look of a boxer.
- I just--

120
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:46,995
- I mean, look at these shoes.
- I just threw them on

121
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:49,164
without thinking about the outfit.

122
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:51,249
- Weren't you punching the sandbag?
- Just some moves

123
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:53,960
- I picked up from dealing with Jonathan.
- I get it.

124
00:04:54,044 --> 00:04:57,297
- Fake boxing.
- Just going through the motions.

125
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:58,590
Are you a decent fighter?

126
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:00,759
- To be honest...
- Are you any good?

127
00:05:00,842 --> 00:05:02,135
- I'm not bad.
- Really?

128
00:05:02,219 --> 00:05:05,013
Then again,
an older brother will take you there.

129
00:05:05,055 --> 00:05:06,515
Even as a little girl,

130
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:09,226
I received training constantly.

131
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:10,435
Have you ever beaten him?

132
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:12,020
Of course not.

133
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:15,857
Not at all, but I have a story.

134
00:05:15,899 --> 00:05:19,402
When I was in elementary school,
Jonathan punched me.

135
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:22,405
How mean. Why would he do that to you?

136
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:24,032
Looking back, I did cross the line.

137
00:05:24,074 --> 00:05:26,952
- Still.
- I spat into his milk tea.

138
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,246
A LITTLE TOO EXTRA

139
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:31,665
I probably deserved it.

140
00:05:31,873 --> 00:05:33,083
Are you okay?

141
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,334
FAINT

142
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:35,460
I spat in his drink.

143
00:05:35,544 --> 00:05:37,003
I made fun of him, too.

144
00:05:37,087 --> 00:05:38,004
Jonathan warned me,

145
00:05:38,088 --> 00:05:40,257
"Cross the line one more time,

146
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:42,259
<i>and I'll beat you up."</i>

147
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,010
- But I--
- Did you make fun of him again?

148
00:05:44,094 --> 00:05:46,096
I was like, "Hit me if you can."

149
00:05:46,179 --> 00:05:48,515
I kept teasing him for a few seconds

150
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:49,933
until he actually hit me.

151
00:05:49,975 --> 00:05:51,601
He threw a punch.

152
00:05:51,643 --> 00:05:54,437
- But I was stubborn.
- That must've hurt.

153
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:56,189
- You played it cool?
- I went, "That didn't hurt."

154
00:05:56,273 --> 00:05:57,983
- But after that,
- "You call it a punch?"

155
00:05:58,233 --> 00:06:00,944
- you went to your room and cried?
- I didn't make it to my room.

156
00:06:00,986 --> 00:06:02,320
It only took me ten seconds

157
00:06:02,404 --> 00:06:03,655
- before I started crying.
- You cried?

158
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:04,573
WAILING

159
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:05,657
I cried my eyes out.

160
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,617
I FEEL YOU 100%

161
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:09,828
That's why my face is asymmetrical.

162
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,496
WHAT A SAD STORY

163
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,540
Is he a few years older than you?

164
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:14,624
By three years?

165
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:16,376
- He's older by two years.
- Right.

166
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:17,878
My brother and I are just a year apart.

167
00:06:17,961 --> 00:06:19,379
- Really?
- So growing up,

168
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:22,257
we were about the same size
when we were little.

169
00:06:22,299 --> 00:06:25,010
- Really?
- So if I gave it my all,

170
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:25,927
we were evenly matched.

171
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:28,471
But when we started middle school,
I couldn't beat him.

172
00:06:28,555 --> 00:06:31,558
Do siblings fight a lot
when they're only one year apart?

173
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:33,018
You have no idea.

174
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:34,769
What did you fight over?

175
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,688
Things like ice cream and...

176
00:06:37,272 --> 00:06:38,481
That's cute.

177
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:39,649
We fought over the remote control.

178
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:41,651
After school,

179
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:43,695
I had to rush home

180
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:45,822
to grab the remote first.
You get it, right?

181
00:06:45,864 --> 00:06:47,782
- You're so brilliant.
- I'd be praying

182
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,409
for my homeroom teacher to dismiss us.

183
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:50,577
An absolute strategist.

184
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:52,245
When the teacher dismissed us,

185
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:55,165
I grabbed my indoor shoes bag

186
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:57,918
<i>- and raced home.</i>
<i>- Did Jonathan also run?</i>

187
00:06:58,001 --> 00:06:59,252
<i>Even now, I have to get home early</i>

188
00:06:59,336 --> 00:07:01,588
because he gave me a curfew.

189
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:03,006
- What's wrong with him?
- I know.

190
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:05,967
- He's unbelievable.
- I don't get what's gotten into him.

191
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:08,011
A 25-year-old can take care of herself.

192
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:09,179
I know, right?

193
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:10,931
I'm 25, for crying out loud.

194
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:13,475
Can you believe
I have to worry about curfew?

195
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:15,018
It's unusual for a brother
to give you a curfew.

196
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:17,062
He must really care about you.

197
00:07:18,355 --> 00:07:20,273
I'm not sure if it's a good thing.

198
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:22,067
- Hello.
- Hello.

199
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,110
NO MORE CHIT-CHAT, THE COACH IS HERE

200
00:07:24,194 --> 00:07:25,862
- Hello.
- Goodness, hello.

201
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:27,197
ESPECIALLY POLITE
Hello, Coach.

202
00:07:27,238 --> 00:07:29,366
I'll be helping you
with your training today.

203
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:31,034
My name is Choi Jae-doo.

204
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:32,452
It's nice to meet you.

205
00:07:32,869 --> 00:07:34,704
Coach Choi Ja-doo.

206
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:37,457
Wait, really? That's a cute name.

207
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:39,334
- That's your name, right?
- Do you know the cartoon?

208
00:07:39,376 --> 00:07:40,502
- "Hey, Ja-doo."
- It's Jae-doo.

209
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:41,628
- Sorry?
- It's Jae-doo.

210
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:43,380
- My apologies.
- Patricia.

211
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:44,464
SORRY

212
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:46,800
- I swear I heard "Choi Ja-doo."
- How could you?

213
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:48,885
- Sorry, the headband's covering my ears.
- Patricia.

214
00:07:48,969 --> 00:07:50,095
I'm sorry.

215
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:51,554
OFFICIAL APOLOGY

216
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:53,723
- It muffled the sound.
- I get it.

217
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:55,517
I see you're both wearing boxing shoes.

218
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,102
WONHEE IS BAREFOOT
Can I get a pair, too?

219
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:58,728
About the shoes.

220
00:07:58,812 --> 00:08:01,731
I didn't realize
there were shoes for boxing.

221
00:08:01,773 --> 00:08:02,899
It's my first time seeing them.

222
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:05,193
- Same here.
- Oh, so the shoes...

223
00:08:05,235 --> 00:08:07,278
Boxing is an indoor sport,

224
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:10,657
- there are shoe regulations for matches.
- Really?

225
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:12,575
Dang, I look legit.

226
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:14,160
- You know...
- Yes?

227
00:08:14,244 --> 00:08:15,495
Your brother, Jonathan...

228
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:17,205
I'm a big fan of his videos.

229
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:18,498
You're with Patricia, though.

230
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:20,625
- But I'm Patricia.
- Of course.

231
00:08:20,709 --> 00:08:22,711
As for compliments to Jonathan,

232
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:24,963
you can tell him
when you see him in person.

233
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:26,589
FLUSTERED
Oh, sure. It's just...

234
00:08:26,631 --> 00:08:28,091
Am I his messenger now?

235
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:29,467
I just wanted to say I'm his fan.

236
00:08:29,551 --> 00:08:31,761
- They have great chemistry.
- Exactly.

237
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:33,346
I also enjoyed <i>Screening Humanity</i>.

238
00:08:33,430 --> 00:08:35,015
Right, their episode was great.

239
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:37,517
Of all the things to watch...

240
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,476
Just kidding.

241
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:41,062
- You're really...
- Yes?

242
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:42,188
TWO THUMBS UP

243
00:08:42,272 --> 00:08:43,606
My gosh, Coach.

244
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:45,066
Your laugh, Patricia.

245
00:08:45,108 --> 00:08:47,777
Your laugh is something else.

246
00:08:47,861 --> 00:08:49,362
It's so clear and loud.

247
00:08:49,446 --> 00:08:51,948
You can almost break
the sound down to syllables.

248
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:54,951
It's funny how we're all talking
about different subjects.

249
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:57,287
JONATHAN, PATRICIA'S LAUGH,
COACH'S THUMBS-UP

250
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,497
- Can you handle all this energy?
- Sure.

251
00:08:59,581 --> 00:09:00,957
EMBARRASSED TWO THUMBS-UP
You like it?

252
00:09:00,999 --> 00:09:01,833
Totally.

253
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:05,128
HAHAHA

254
00:09:06,296 --> 00:09:07,797
I don't know why this is so funny.

255
00:09:07,839 --> 00:09:09,466
Why are you this funny?

256
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,468
- Can we get started?
- Oh, sure.

257
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:12,802
- Do you need more time?
- Let's stop here.

258
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:14,554
- Let's do this.
- All right.

259
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:17,140
- We'll get started.
- All right.

260
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:19,309
Before we begin,

261
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,478
- we'll do a warm-up.
- Yes, sir.

262
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:24,481
For starters, stand up straight.

263
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:25,774
Stretch out your glutes.

264
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:27,650
Knee up high.

265
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:29,319
We'll do an eight-count stretch.

266
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,821
One, two, three, four.

267
00:09:32,989 --> 00:09:35,784
- This isn't so bad.
- Five, six, seven, eight.

268
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:36,659
- Switch feet.
- Wait.

269
00:09:36,743 --> 00:09:39,329
You said "eight-count" in English,
then counted in Korean.

270
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:43,458
I was ready to count in English,
but he started in Korean.

271
00:09:43,917 --> 00:09:44,793
It was almost...

272
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:47,170
- One, two, three, four.
- Let's just stretch.

273
00:09:47,212 --> 00:09:49,589
Five, six, seven, eight.

274
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:51,091
Great.

275
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:52,842
Next, we're going to work on our quads.

276
00:09:52,884 --> 00:09:54,511
Bend your knee and hold the position.

277
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:56,554
The other leg has to keep you grounded.

278
00:09:56,638 --> 00:09:59,265
One, two, three, four.

279
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:01,768
- It's not so bad so far.
- Five, six, seven, eight.

280
00:10:02,102 --> 00:10:05,438
THEY CONTINUE ON

281
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:07,023
TO STRETCH THOROUGHLY

282
00:10:07,065 --> 00:10:08,316
Okay, then.

283
00:10:08,358 --> 00:10:11,277
As you inhale, expand your chest.

284
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:12,362
DEEP BREATH IN

285
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:14,614
As you exhale, relax.

286
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:15,698
One more time.

287
00:10:17,659 --> 00:10:18,910
HAHAHA
Exhale.

288
00:10:19,202 --> 00:10:21,579
Good job. Well done, everyone.

289
00:10:21,663 --> 00:10:24,040
We'll stretch out our hamstrings.

290
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:25,041
ONE MORE TIME

291
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:27,043
- Okay, I'll be quiet.
- Bring your feet...

292
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:30,380
This is harder than I thought.

293
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:31,464
So moving on...

294
00:10:32,549 --> 00:10:33,716
Sorry.

295
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,885
- May I continue?
- You've got this!

296
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:38,054
- Let's go, Ja-doo.
- Bring your feet together.

297
00:10:38,096 --> 00:10:41,891
Bring one foot forward and stretch.

298
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:43,143
Like this?

299
00:10:43,226 --> 00:10:44,144
SO SEXY

300
00:10:44,227 --> 00:10:46,521
- Am I doing this right?
- Oh, well...

301
00:10:46,563 --> 00:10:49,858
Our goal is to stretch out
the muscles behind your thigh.

302
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:51,276
- I get it.
- It's working now.

303
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:53,319
Do I say "yum" when I feel the burn?

304
00:10:53,403 --> 00:10:54,404
What?

305
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:55,738
INQUISITIVE 20-YEAR-OLD

306
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:58,032
Twentysomethings are always curious.
Don't panic.

307
00:10:58,074 --> 00:11:00,201
- Don't people say that at the gym?
- They do.

308
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:01,911
- Whenever they feel it, "Yum!"
- "Yum!"

309
00:11:01,995 --> 00:11:03,288
WHEN THE MUSCLES KICK IN

310
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:04,914
Gym rats go, "Yum!"

311
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:06,374
"Yum!"

312
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:07,584
Let's move on.

313
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:08,459
OVERWHELMED

314
00:11:08,543 --> 00:11:10,837
SAD
One, two, three, four.

315
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,256
- I hope he doesn't run away.
- Five, six, seven, eight.

316
00:11:13,298 --> 00:11:14,591
The other side.

317
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:17,427
- One, two, three, four.
- Yum.

318
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:18,720
...seven, eight.

319
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,013
I'm hot and exhausted already.

320
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:22,098
That was a lot. Can we take five?

321
00:11:22,182 --> 00:11:24,517
- Let's get some water.
- Today won't be easy.

322
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:26,978
That's a wrap on warm-up stretching.

323
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:29,856
- That was only the warm-up?
- Right.

324
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:32,775
- When do we start punching?
- With every workout,

325
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,278
you need a proper warm-up.

326
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:38,239
Why don't we get started
with a few jumping jacks?

327
00:11:38,281 --> 00:11:39,908
We'll do just 20.

328
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:41,951
"Just 20"?

329
00:11:42,035 --> 00:11:43,203
- Understood.
- One more thing.

330
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:45,622
Jump high and clap overhead.

331
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:46,497
- Okay.
- High?

332
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:48,458
What if we hit the ceiling?

333
00:11:48,541 --> 00:11:50,418
- What happens then?
- If you get hurt,

334
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:53,004
we can cover any cost
with the gym's insurance.

335
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:55,048
What about my pain?

336
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:58,301
I wasn't asking about damage to the gym.

337
00:11:58,343 --> 00:12:00,511
- I'd be hurt.
- Oh, I get it.

338
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:03,181
- Why don't you try jumping?
- I think I can reach it.

339
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:05,391
One, two, three!

340
00:12:05,475 --> 00:12:06,684
TOUCHED

341
00:12:09,771 --> 00:12:11,606
- Let's give it a go.
- Okay.

342
00:12:11,648 --> 00:12:12,607
Ready, go.

343
00:12:12,649 --> 00:12:14,484
- One, two, three.
- One!

344
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:16,319
- One, two, three.
- Two!

345
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:18,321
- One, two, three.
- Why aren't you doing it with us?

346
00:12:18,363 --> 00:12:19,530
- Come on!
- One, two, three.

347
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:20,448
- Five!
- Five!

348
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:22,200
- One, two, three.
- Seven!

349
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,826
- One, two, three.
- Eight!

350
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:25,995
- Let's keep going.
- Nine!

351
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:27,830
- One, two, three.
- Ten!

352
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,749
CHEATING

353
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:31,501
- One, two, three.
- I'm tired!

354
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:33,378
- One, two, three.
- Sixteen!

355
00:12:33,461 --> 00:12:35,088
- One, two, three.
- Twenty!

356
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,464
Great job.

357
00:12:36,506 --> 00:12:37,507
MY EARS HURT

358
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:39,884
Coach...

359
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:41,552
THUMBS-UP AT LAST
You did an excellent job.

360
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:44,180
ABOUT TO THROW UP

361
00:12:45,223 --> 00:12:46,391
WAIT, YOUR TOP

362
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:49,227
Oh, thank you.

363
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:50,687
Was that too much for you?

364
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:52,230
- No, we're fine.
- Are you?

365
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:54,274
We're just catching our breath.

366
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:56,025
We're taking a break, that's all.

367
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:57,902
JUST A LITTLE BREAK

368
00:12:57,986 --> 00:12:59,988
Next up are burpees.

369
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,990
Burpees? I've never heard of it.

370
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:04,867
Let me show you how it's done.

371
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,161
Put your hands on the floor
and kick your feet back.

372
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:09,539
Come back up and jump. That's one rep.

373
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,082
- Okay.
- Would you like to see again?

374
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:13,084
- Yes, please.
- All right. One, two, three.

375
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:15,628
- You're good at this, Coach.
- One more time.

376
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:17,171
One, two, three.

377
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:18,589
YOU'RE THE BEST, COACH

378
00:13:18,673 --> 00:13:19,841
So that's how it's done.

379
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:21,009
We've got this, right?

380
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:23,303
Let's just do six burpees
to get warmed up.

381
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:24,220
Are you ready?

382
00:13:24,262 --> 00:13:25,888
- Yes!
- That's the spirit.

383
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,265
Ready, go.

384
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:29,726
- One, two, three. One!
- One!

385
00:13:29,809 --> 00:13:32,228
- One, two, three. Two!
- Two!

386
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:34,522
TWO ARE IN SYNC

387
00:13:34,564 --> 00:13:35,690
Come on.

388
00:13:35,732 --> 00:13:37,859
BUT PATRICIA ISN'T

389
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:39,944
- One, two, three. Five!
- Coach, please!

390
00:13:40,028 --> 00:13:41,154
- One last time!
- Five!

391
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:42,322
One, two, three.

392
00:13:42,405 --> 00:13:44,657
THE END

393
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:46,242
Good job, Patricia.

394
00:13:46,284 --> 00:13:47,744
I jumped like a frog.

395
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:51,080
You were perfect. I saw your form.

396
00:13:51,122 --> 00:13:52,790
- That wasn't easy.
- Right.

397
00:13:52,874 --> 00:13:54,584
DOUBLE THUMBS-UP
Thanks for hanging in there.

398
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:57,378
So that was a simple warm-up exercise.

399
00:13:57,420 --> 00:13:58,671
- Okay.
- "Simple"?

400
00:13:58,755 --> 00:14:02,258
To check your stamina,
we'll try battle ropes.

401
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:03,676
- That?
- You mean this?

402
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:05,928
- Do we have to swing the ropes?
- Exactly.

403
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:07,180
I've never tried it.

404
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:08,765
Could you help, Coach Kim?

405
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:10,183
Are you also a coach?

406
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:11,267
He must be.

407
00:14:11,351 --> 00:14:13,436
Hello, Coach.

408
00:14:13,478 --> 00:14:16,272
ENTERS WITH BATTLE ROPES
Hello.

409
00:14:16,314 --> 00:14:17,857
COACH KIM HYUN-GI
This tests explosive power

410
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,109
- more than endurance.
- I see.

411
00:14:20,193 --> 00:14:22,987
Put as much power into it as you can.

412
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:24,405
With feet shoulder-width apart...

413
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:25,573
Okay.

414
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:28,159
Send the waves all the way to the end.

415
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,452
- All the way to...
- Like this.

416
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:30,453
WAVES

417
00:14:30,495 --> 00:14:31,996
You're awesome, Coach!

418
00:14:33,164 --> 00:14:33,998
All right.

419
00:14:34,082 --> 00:14:35,792
- We'll time 30 seconds.
- What?

420
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,085
- Well, I mean...
- What?

421
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:39,670
- For his demo.
- The 30 seconds for the demo?

422
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:41,130
YAY

423
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:43,257
READS THE ROOM
How about 20 seconds for you?

424
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:44,967
PATRICIA IS HAPPY
Or 10 seconds?

425
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:47,136
- Good luck, Coach Kim!
- Let's see a demonstration.

426
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:49,555
- You could get hurt, so step back a bit.
- Step back.

427
00:14:49,639 --> 00:14:50,515
Step back, everyone.

428
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:53,684
- You're putting pressure on him.
- Stay back for your safety.

429
00:14:53,768 --> 00:14:54,977
THE PRESSURE IS ON

430
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:56,896
- So cool!
- He's rolled up his sleeves.

431
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:58,314
Ready, go.

432
00:14:58,356 --> 00:14:59,440
ROPES RIPPLING VIGOROUSLY

433
00:14:59,482 --> 00:15:00,775
Wow, so strong.

434
00:15:00,817 --> 00:15:02,652
Keep it going. Just a bit harder.

435
00:15:02,735 --> 00:15:04,320
Way to go.

436
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:06,114
More.

437
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:08,157
Keep the waves going.

438
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:11,869
- How much time is left?
- He has 13 seconds.

439
00:15:11,953 --> 00:15:13,329
- Go, Coach Kim!
- Ten seconds now.

440
00:15:13,371 --> 00:15:16,332
WE ARE CHEERING FOR YOU

441
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:17,542
GIVING IT EVERYTHING

442
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:19,669
- You're amazing.
- One.

443
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:21,045
Stop.

444
00:15:21,129 --> 00:15:22,380
- Just wow.
- Incredible.

445
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:25,842
- Why are we tired?
- I don't know.

446
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:28,970
Even ten seconds looks hard.

447
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:30,221
It's your turn now.

448
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:33,724
As the older trainee today,
I'd like to volunteer...

449
00:15:33,808 --> 00:15:34,892
Just ten seconds?

450
00:15:34,976 --> 00:15:37,019
...to go after Wonhee.

451
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:38,312
- What?
- You can go first.

452
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:39,397
I SEE

453
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,190
Why don't you go first, Wonhee?

454
00:15:41,232 --> 00:15:44,193
- I just--
- I'd like to go after Patricia

455
00:15:44,235 --> 00:15:45,736
so I can watch and learn.

456
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:46,696
Is that right?

457
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:48,823
- Okay, I'll go first.
- Rock-paper-scissors?

458
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:49,991
GIRLIE GOES FIRST

459
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:51,659
We have a lot to cover,

460
00:15:51,701 --> 00:15:53,369
- so I'll give you ten seconds.
- Got it.

461
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:55,163
FIRST CHALLENGER, PATRICIA

462
00:15:56,122 --> 00:15:58,249
APPROXIMATELY 7.2KG
These are heavier than I thought.

463
00:15:58,332 --> 00:15:59,250
Are you ready?

464
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:00,877
Do I just swing them?

465
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,045
Yes, alternate your arms like this.

466
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,213
Have fun with them.

467
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:07,467
GIGGLES

468
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:09,218
- Remember
- The ropes are pulling me.

469
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:11,012
- to send the waves all the way down.
- Got it.

470
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:12,305
Use your legs.

471
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:14,390
Oh, so I put my legs like this?

472
00:16:14,474 --> 00:16:15,475
Engaging my legs.

473
00:16:15,558 --> 00:16:16,601
Let's go.

474
00:16:16,851 --> 00:16:18,227
Ready, go.

475
00:16:18,269 --> 00:16:19,353
START

476
00:16:19,395 --> 00:16:20,646
POWERED BY HER BATTLE CRY

477
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:22,356
Until the end.

478
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:26,235
Hang on, Coach!

479
00:16:28,154 --> 00:16:30,573
- What on earth?
- One. There.

480
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:32,575
- You did great.
- This is just...

481
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:34,160
- It's terrible.
- Is it that bad?

482
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:36,787
Really? She says it's terrible.

483
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:38,831
How did you last 30 seconds?

484
00:16:38,915 --> 00:16:40,500
We have high hopes for Wonhee.

485
00:16:40,583 --> 00:16:41,626
- So heavy.
- You've got this!

486
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,252
- Okay.
- Good luck!

487
00:16:43,294 --> 00:16:45,087
- Engage your legs.
- Legs engaged.

488
00:16:45,129 --> 00:16:46,547
Swing them just once. Go.

489
00:16:46,589 --> 00:16:48,508
Alternate your arms.

490
00:16:48,591 --> 00:16:50,259
- Don't get dragged forward.
- Wonhee.

491
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:51,844
WILL SHE BE OKAY?

492
00:16:51,928 --> 00:16:54,347
Just ten seconds. Ready, go.

493
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:55,515
START

494
00:16:55,598 --> 00:16:57,099
- You're good.
- Keep it going.

495
00:16:57,183 --> 00:16:59,060
- Make bigger waves.
- You're incredible.

496
00:16:59,101 --> 00:17:00,645
Way to go, Wonhee!

497
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:02,688
- Three, two...
- Wow, you're on fire.

498
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:04,565
GUINEA PIG GOING FULL POWER

499
00:17:04,607 --> 00:17:06,567
Okay, great job.

500
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:08,611
- I'm exhausted.
- Well done.

501
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:11,489
The funny thing is,
we haven't even begun the real thing.

502
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:12,615
It's only a warm-up.

503
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,283
RUNNING AWAY FROM REALITY

504
00:17:14,325 --> 00:17:16,285
We'll get started on boxing.

505
00:17:16,369 --> 00:17:19,205
Before we do, we'll wrap your hands.

506
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:21,332
ROCKY SOUNDTRACK

507
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:23,876
Are you familiar with hand wraps?

508
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,836
- I'll give you a rundown.
- Thank you.

509
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:30,091
The hand wraps protect
your knuckles and your wrists.

510
00:17:30,258 --> 00:17:32,260
This is pretty cool.

511
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,262
I feel like an actual boxer.

512
00:17:34,637 --> 00:17:36,013
Spread out your fingers like this.

513
00:17:36,097 --> 00:17:38,641
- Okay.
- If it's too tight, it might hurt.

514
00:17:39,267 --> 00:17:40,643
- You're all set.
- Thank you.

515
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:42,979
- There we go.
- Thank you.

516
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:45,273
My nemesis during elementary school.

517
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:46,899
Jump rope.

518
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:48,359
I can do triple-unders.

519
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:50,194
- Seriously?
- Of course.

520
00:17:50,278 --> 00:17:52,238
Each round of boxing

521
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:54,365
is a 3-minute sparring
and a 1-minute break.

522
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:57,827
So we'll try the same exercise
for three minutes

523
00:17:57,910 --> 00:17:59,787
and take a one-minute break.

524
00:17:59,829 --> 00:18:02,915
So we're jumping rope for 1 minute
and resting for 3?

525
00:18:02,999 --> 00:18:04,667
- No, the opposite.
- Really?

526
00:18:05,376 --> 00:18:07,837
AMAZED
That was so smooth.

527
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:09,839
I was trying to be clever.

528
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,299
When you hear the ding,

529
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,134
- start turning the rope.
- Right away?

530
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:15,636
Even if you trip, keep going.

531
00:18:15,678 --> 00:18:18,973
- Can I do double-unders--
- Sure, feel free to try triple-unders.

532
00:18:19,015 --> 00:18:21,017
Won't you cut down 30 seconds for that?

533
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,560
I'm afraid I can't.

534
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:25,396
- Understood.
- Let's get started. Ready.

535
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:29,191
START

536
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:30,735
Good.

537
00:18:34,071 --> 00:18:35,448
This isn't easy.

538
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:37,199
How about a double-under, Wonhee?

539
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:38,409
- Me?
- Yes.

540
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:39,910
Oh, well...

541
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:42,788
- I'm building momentum. Give me a second.
- What?

542
00:18:42,872 --> 00:18:44,665
BUILDING MOMENTUM

543
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,712
PERFECT DOUBLE-UNDERS
That's cool.

544
00:18:49,754 --> 00:18:50,588
Thank you.

545
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:52,131
You're so cool.

546
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:53,716
I am, right?

547
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:54,842
No talking.

548
00:18:54,884 --> 00:18:56,719
HEHE

549
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,888
High five. We're doing great.

550
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:00,222
- Just incredible.
- Skrr, skrr.

551
00:19:00,306 --> 00:19:01,891
EXCHANGING COMPLIMENTS
You're something else.

552
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:04,143
It takes up more energy
than you might think.

553
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:08,105
Even young trainees want to take
a breather now and then.

554
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,650
So I have to be there to... Wait.

555
00:19:10,733 --> 00:19:12,234
YOUNG TRAINEE TAKES A BREAK

556
00:19:12,318 --> 00:19:13,235
Wonhee!

557
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:15,237
Pull it together, Wonhee.

558
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:17,198
You've got this!

559
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:19,825
Where are you, Wonhee?

560
00:19:19,909 --> 00:19:21,827
ME?

561
00:19:21,911 --> 00:19:23,412
How much longer?

562
00:19:23,496 --> 00:19:25,790
- You have 1 minute and 27 seconds.
- Maybe 20 seconds?

563
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:27,124
We still have more to go.

564
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:29,794
- Get back to it.
- What the...

565
00:19:29,877 --> 00:19:30,920
- Come on.
- Coach.

566
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:33,047
- Pick up the pace.
- It's been two minutes at least.

567
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:35,925
- You've got this.
- I've got this!

568
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:37,093
WRETCHES

569
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,886
I've got this.

570
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:40,471
With that,

571
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:42,264
we're down to the last minute.

572
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:45,101
At the 30-second mark,
try high-knee jump roping.

573
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:46,435
No way!

574
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,854
Sorry about that.

575
00:19:48,938 --> 00:19:50,106
Sorry.

576
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:51,315
Coach.

577
00:19:51,399 --> 00:19:52,858
This is just...

578
00:19:52,942 --> 00:19:54,985
You'll hear the ding at 30 seconds.

579
00:19:55,486 --> 00:19:56,654
- One.
- My ears are going.

580
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:59,073
Now, start the high-knee jump rope.

581
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:01,534
- Faster now.
- Again.

582
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:03,327
- You go, girl!
- Good job.

583
00:20:03,411 --> 00:20:04,370
WONHEE PULLS IT OFF

584
00:20:04,787 --> 00:20:07,289
Patricia's doing it, too. Great job.

585
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,625
Let's keep it going.

586
00:20:09,709 --> 00:20:11,627
Final ten seconds. Come on.

587
00:20:11,711 --> 00:20:13,587
Keep going. Seven...

588
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:16,424
...three, two, one.

589
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:19,135
COLLAPSING
There we go. Good job.

590
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:20,845
Come on, Coach!

591
00:20:21,262 --> 00:20:23,639
We have a long way to go.
Take a sip of water.

592
00:20:23,723 --> 00:20:28,310
HYDRATION BREAK

593
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:32,064
Boxing is a combat sport
between two opponents.

594
00:20:32,148 --> 00:20:33,691
Let's learn the boxing stances.

595
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:34,859
- Stances?
- Yes.

596
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:36,986
- Place your feet shoulder-width apart.
- Okay.

597
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:38,904
Now, remember your dominant hand

598
00:20:38,988 --> 00:20:40,448
and take your foot on that side back.

599
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,408
- Take it back.
- Hold the pose

600
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:45,828
and turn your body slightly to the side
to stand at an angle.

601
00:20:45,870 --> 00:20:46,954
At an angle.

602
00:20:47,872 --> 00:20:48,998
- This way.
- Okay.

603
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:50,499
- Do I step inside?
- Sure.

604
00:20:50,541 --> 00:20:52,752
- Copy and paste.
- Exactly.

605
00:20:52,835 --> 00:20:53,753
Like this?

606
00:20:55,087 --> 00:20:58,382
Raise your heels. One more thing.

607
00:20:58,466 --> 00:21:00,551
Relax the muscles around your knees

608
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:02,136
and make two thumbs-up.

609
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:03,888
After that,

610
00:21:03,971 --> 00:21:06,515
fold your thumb down
along the side of your fist.

611
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:07,767
Along the side of my fist.

612
00:21:07,850 --> 00:21:11,395
Keep your right fist back as your guard.

613
00:21:11,479 --> 00:21:13,773
Place it next to your nose
and right cheekbone.

614
00:21:14,565 --> 00:21:15,608
So shy.

615
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:17,193
HAHAHA

616
00:21:17,401 --> 00:21:19,236
I feel so shy.

617
00:21:19,570 --> 00:21:21,322
SIDE EFFECTS OF WORKING OUT
I'm losing my mind.

618
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:22,782
DRAINED
You two are...

619
00:21:22,865 --> 00:21:25,993
COACH CHOI'S HALF-HEARTED THUMBS-UP

620
00:21:26,202 --> 00:21:29,371
You're so fond of me, aren't you?
It's getting a little much.

621
00:21:29,413 --> 00:21:31,707
Bring your left hand
to the outer end of your eyebrow.

622
00:21:31,791 --> 00:21:33,709
Move it forward,
leaving about four fists of space.

623
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:36,045
Keep your left fist at your eye level.

624
00:21:38,214 --> 00:21:41,217
Now, hold that pose
as we move on to footwork.

625
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:44,178
- First, we'll learn the front step.
- Front step.

626
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:45,554
Be careful. You got it.

627
00:21:45,596 --> 00:21:47,515
You're good.

628
00:21:47,556 --> 00:21:49,767
We'll also learn
how to shuffle back and forth

629
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,894
like a pendulum.

630
00:21:51,936 --> 00:21:54,605
Let me point out
where people often go wrong.

631
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:56,273
While practicing your footwork,

632
00:21:56,357 --> 00:21:57,900
- you start moving like this.
- So true!

633
00:21:57,942 --> 00:21:59,068
FIXED-TORSO

634
00:21:59,109 --> 00:22:01,153
CORRECT, WRONG

635
00:22:01,487 --> 00:22:03,197
Hold the pose. Ready, go.

636
00:22:03,239 --> 00:22:04,406
FRONT STEP PRACTICE

637
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:05,407
There we go.

638
00:22:06,075 --> 00:22:08,953
Right, this is exactly
what you shouldn't be doing.

639
00:22:09,036 --> 00:22:12,081
We'll be sparring later,
and if your steps are like this...

640
00:22:12,248 --> 00:22:13,999
Her steps are worse than mine!

641
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:15,668
This is idol basics. Watch and learn.

642
00:22:15,751 --> 00:22:18,295
It's a two-step.

643
00:22:18,379 --> 00:22:19,213
Like this.

644
00:22:19,255 --> 00:22:21,257
I'll show you a dance from our new song.

645
00:22:25,344 --> 00:22:26,637
Let's keep it going.

646
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:30,266
Back and forth.

647
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:31,934
Great.

648
00:22:32,268 --> 00:22:33,602
Face forward.

649
00:22:33,644 --> 00:22:35,604
Imagine an opponent in front of you.

650
00:22:37,231 --> 00:22:39,316
Let's move on to punches.

651
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,865
You're here to learn, so...

652
00:22:45,948 --> 00:22:47,283
CONCERNED
Am I pushing them too hard?

653
00:22:47,324 --> 00:22:48,951
- Not at all.
- Right?

654
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:50,286
You're not pushing us.

655
00:22:50,327 --> 00:22:51,579
Not at all.

656
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:52,872
We're fine.

657
00:22:52,955 --> 00:22:54,498
- Can you stand up, please?
- Sure.

658
00:22:54,582 --> 00:22:56,041
Great.

659
00:22:56,125 --> 00:22:57,877
I figured out why I'm so exhausted.

660
00:22:58,127 --> 00:23:00,170
I had a late-night snack yesterday.

661
00:23:00,254 --> 00:23:01,672
- That's bad.
- I was wondering

662
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:03,591
why my body felt so heavy.

663
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:05,634
- I had a fourth meal!
- What did you have?

664
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:07,177
I had a burger.

665
00:23:07,261 --> 00:23:08,971
- It's sitting right here.
- It sure is.

666
00:23:09,013 --> 00:23:11,390
The exercises they've been doing

667
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:13,642
are very challenging for beginners.

668
00:23:13,726 --> 00:23:17,313
Our trainees here have been doing great.

669
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:20,733
- Thank you. Nice.
- The viewers at home shouldn't think

670
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:22,651
- that they're overreacting.
- Exactly.

671
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:24,320
ROAR
Try it yourself.

672
00:23:24,361 --> 00:23:26,488
- Try it yourself!
- Come and try it.

673
00:23:26,572 --> 00:23:28,157
Let's learn how to throw a jab.

674
00:23:28,198 --> 00:23:30,868
- We're going to start throwing punches.
- I've heard of that.

675
00:23:34,663 --> 00:23:36,248
CALM DOWN, PLEASE

676
00:23:36,332 --> 00:23:37,249
All right.

677
00:23:37,333 --> 00:23:40,085
To throw a jab, first raise your fists.

678
00:23:40,169 --> 00:23:41,253
Fists are up.

679
00:23:41,337 --> 00:23:43,255
Extend your fist forward,
then bring it back.

680
00:23:43,339 --> 00:23:45,424
Let me point out a common mistake.

681
00:23:45,507 --> 00:23:49,511
People trying to punch hard
often push their shoulder forward.

682
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,513
Never lose your balance.

683
00:23:51,722 --> 00:23:53,682
When your whole arm moves...

684
00:23:53,766 --> 00:23:55,684
You might go, "Stop it already."

685
00:23:55,726 --> 00:23:56,602
You nailed it, Coach.

686
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,103
- That's exactly it.
- "Stop it."

687
00:23:58,187 --> 00:24:00,439
That happens when you lose your balance.

688
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:02,149
Your shoulder moves
because you're trying too hard.

689
00:24:02,191 --> 00:24:04,234
Enough, okay?

690
00:24:05,361 --> 00:24:07,029
The key in boxing

691
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:09,698
- is even weight distribution.
- An even balance.

692
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:10,616
When throwing a punch,

693
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:13,786
turn your arm
so your knuckles land the hit.

694
00:24:13,994 --> 00:24:15,955
- Knuckles.
- Now put your guard up.

695
00:24:16,038 --> 00:24:17,539
Let me see you try it. Ready.

696
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:19,416
- To the front.
- Ready, go.

697
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:20,960
JAB PRACTICE

698
00:24:21,043 --> 00:24:21,877
There you go.

699
00:24:21,919 --> 00:24:22,878
Jab. Okay.

700
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:26,215
Your jab isn't reaching.

701
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:27,132
One more time.

702
00:24:27,216 --> 00:24:28,217
One more.

703
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:29,468
One more. You're doing great,

704
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:31,845
- but your back foot is dragging.
- Really?

705
00:24:31,887 --> 00:24:35,557
Because your balance is off,
your jabs can't reach the target.

706
00:24:35,599 --> 00:24:37,726
- You're next, buddy.
- Yes?

707
00:24:37,768 --> 00:24:39,144
He's calling me "buddy" now.

708
00:24:39,228 --> 00:24:40,396
I'm tired!

709
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:42,648
Give it a go. Ready, go.

710
00:24:44,066 --> 00:24:45,651
Her jab is next-level.

711
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:46,568
A whole new level.

712
00:24:46,735 --> 00:24:48,946
I'm so jealous. Dang it.

713
00:24:49,029 --> 00:24:50,072
I'm going to train, too.

714
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:51,365
COMPETITIVE MODE ACTIVATED

715
00:24:51,407 --> 00:24:53,909
That was great,
but you made the common mistake

716
00:24:53,993 --> 00:24:56,078
ONLY MOVING FROM THE HIPS DOWN
<i>of shuffling your legs only.</i>

717
00:24:56,161 --> 00:24:59,289
Always remember to move your whole body.

718
00:24:59,373 --> 00:25:01,250
You must remember that.

719
00:25:01,291 --> 00:25:03,252
- Hold up your hand.
- All right.

720
00:25:03,293 --> 00:25:04,586
- Let's go, buddy.
- All right.

721
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:05,713
Ready, go.

722
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:07,089
NEW DETERMINATION

723
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:08,590
I can feel the difference.

724
00:25:08,674 --> 00:25:11,552
- I'm doing better, right?
- You definitely improved.

725
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:14,263
- She's good.
- You've got a competitive spirit.

726
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:17,891
Great job.

727
00:25:19,935 --> 00:25:21,979
Let's try a one-two combo.

728
00:25:22,062 --> 00:25:23,897
WHAT IS THAT?

729
00:25:23,939 --> 00:25:27,443
A one-two combo is
a jab followed by a straight.

730
00:25:27,526 --> 00:25:30,446
Hold after throwing a jab.

731
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:33,073
There we go. Now, another key point.

732
00:25:33,115 --> 00:25:35,325
Your back foot should turn outward.

733
00:25:35,409 --> 00:25:38,370
Twist around and find a balance.

734
00:25:38,454 --> 00:25:39,621
There you go.

735
00:25:39,663 --> 00:25:41,248
- Move your back foot.
- But my left hand...

736
00:25:41,290 --> 00:25:42,708
Just a bit more.

737
00:25:42,791 --> 00:25:43,792
- To here?
- Exactly.

738
00:25:43,876 --> 00:25:45,919
- Easy to find a balance?
- Yes.

739
00:25:45,961 --> 00:25:46,920
You too, Patricia.

740
00:25:47,504 --> 00:25:49,965
Next, turn your back foot
and throw a straight.

741
00:25:50,007 --> 00:25:51,091
Pow. There we go.

742
00:25:51,133 --> 00:25:52,634
Well done. Just one thing.

743
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:54,303
Your whole torso moves forward.

744
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,847
- That way, you lose your balance.
- Right.

745
00:25:56,930 --> 00:25:59,308
Then you can't transition
into the next move.

746
00:25:59,349 --> 00:26:00,517
After throwing a jab,

747
00:26:00,601 --> 00:26:05,355
your body should stick to the center axis
and just twist it.

748
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:07,608
There you go. Marvelous.

749
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:09,985
Let me see you try the one-two combo.

750
00:26:15,157 --> 00:26:16,492
- One last time.
- Okay.

751
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:21,705
This time, connect the moves

752
00:26:21,789 --> 00:26:23,123
- into a one-two combo.
- All right.

753
00:26:23,165 --> 00:26:24,458
Give me a one-two.

754
00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:28,504
Coach?

755
00:26:28,545 --> 00:26:30,339
When you say, "one-two," do we punch?

756
00:26:30,422 --> 00:26:32,216
- Pow, pow. Got it?
- I get it now.

757
00:26:32,299 --> 00:26:33,801
Teach us the rhythm.

758
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:34,968
PERFECTLY UNDERSTOOD NOW

759
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:36,720
Pow, pow.

760
00:26:36,804 --> 00:26:37,638
Now.

761
00:26:38,472 --> 00:26:39,556
- Pow, pow.
- Pow, pow.

762
00:26:40,516 --> 00:26:42,101
CONFIDENCE REGAINED

763
00:26:42,184 --> 00:26:43,143
- Pow, pow.
- Pow, pow.

764
00:26:44,311 --> 00:26:45,395
One more time.

765
00:26:45,479 --> 00:26:46,647
- Pow, pow.
- Amazing.

766
00:26:47,648 --> 00:26:50,692
I think you're ready for mitt training.

767
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:52,778
Coaches, please help them with the gloves.

768
00:26:52,861 --> 00:26:54,822
We finally get gloves!

769
00:26:54,863 --> 00:26:55,906
Gloves!

770
00:26:55,989 --> 00:26:57,699
Who wants to go first?

771
00:26:57,741 --> 00:26:59,493
- Go ahead, Wonhee. I went first earlier.
- Me?

772
00:26:59,535 --> 00:27:00,619
Okay, I'm ready.

773
00:27:00,702 --> 00:27:02,704
Assume your stance.

774
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:05,415
WONHEE IS READY

775
00:27:05,499 --> 00:27:08,502
Can you set the timer to 2 minutes?
I don't think they can last 3.

776
00:27:08,544 --> 00:27:10,504
That's true.

777
00:27:10,546 --> 00:27:11,880
We'll train for two minutes.

778
00:27:11,964 --> 00:27:14,550
Fair enough. He saw right through us.

779
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:17,052
- Your left hand should hit my left.
- My left hand...

780
00:27:17,094 --> 00:27:17,970
- Jab.
- Good job.

781
00:27:18,053 --> 00:27:19,054
Bring your right fist here.

782
00:27:19,138 --> 00:27:20,889
- My right fist goes here.
- Right.

783
00:27:20,973 --> 00:27:23,392
Let me see your one-two combo. Ready, go.

784
00:27:23,809 --> 00:27:25,269
PERFECT FOOTWORK

785
00:27:25,352 --> 00:27:26,520
Good job. She's a natural.

786
00:27:27,104 --> 00:27:28,021
Gosh, Wonhee.

787
00:27:28,063 --> 00:27:30,065
She's ready for a match.

788
00:27:30,107 --> 00:27:31,817
I can take all of...

789
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:32,734
FEISTY PUNCHES

790
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:34,486
Who let loose a kitten here?

791
00:27:35,571 --> 00:27:36,738
Let's see her try it.

792
00:27:36,822 --> 00:27:38,073
Hit the buzzer.

793
00:27:38,157 --> 00:27:40,159
- Good luck! You're amazing.
- I've got this!

794
00:27:40,242 --> 00:27:41,493
- Ready. Take a bow.
- Wonhee!

795
00:27:41,577 --> 00:27:42,452
PRE-FIGHT BOW

796
00:27:42,536 --> 00:27:44,079
- Assume your stance.
- Oh, we bow first?

797
00:27:44,163 --> 00:27:45,205
Practice your footwork.

798
00:27:45,247 --> 00:27:46,456
Great.

799
00:27:46,540 --> 00:27:48,375
A NEW FIRE IN HER EYES

800
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:51,962
- Just a jab.
- Just a jab?

801
00:27:52,045 --> 00:27:53,380
Wait, the one-two combo is this.

802
00:27:53,422 --> 00:27:55,090
DON'T FORGET THE ONE-TWO POW-POW

803
00:27:55,132 --> 00:27:56,258
Shift your weight.

804
00:27:58,051 --> 00:27:59,386
There. Finish with a back step.

805
00:27:59,428 --> 00:28:01,263
- You're doing great.
- Do I step back after the jab?

806
00:28:01,305 --> 00:28:03,056
Yes, that's because your jab

807
00:28:03,098 --> 00:28:04,308
- will be followed--
- By a counter?

808
00:28:04,391 --> 00:28:05,559
Right, they will counter.

809
00:28:05,601 --> 00:28:06,685
I have to dodge right away.

810
00:28:06,768 --> 00:28:08,103
SLIPPING AWAY
Exactly.

811
00:28:08,187 --> 00:28:10,731
You can't hit me.

812
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:12,232
Like a cute little squirrel.

813
00:28:12,274 --> 00:28:13,442
Let's get back to work!

814
00:28:13,525 --> 00:28:15,277
Back and forth we go.

815
00:28:16,778 --> 00:28:17,779
All right. Good job.

816
00:28:17,821 --> 00:28:19,698
TURNING HER BACK FOOT
This isn't easy.

817
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:21,450
It's not as easy as practice.

818
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:24,912
It's harder when you have to keep moving.

819
00:28:24,953 --> 00:28:27,289
Punching while standing still
and hitting a moving target

820
00:28:27,331 --> 00:28:30,125
- are completely different.
- It's so much harder.

821
00:28:30,834 --> 00:28:32,461
- Oops, I lost the rhythm.
- Yes, the rhythm.

822
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:33,754
- One, two. One.
- One, two. One.

823
00:28:33,795 --> 00:28:34,922
So adorable.

824
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:36,506
- Get moving!
- One.

825
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:37,841
One, two, three.

826
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:39,968
Great job.

827
00:28:40,052 --> 00:28:41,678
Okay, one last practice.

828
00:28:41,762 --> 00:28:43,639
We'll finish with five reps.

829
00:28:43,722 --> 00:28:45,474
One-two. Back step. One.

830
00:28:45,515 --> 00:28:48,268
One-two. Back step. Two.
Let's do five of these.

831
00:28:48,310 --> 00:28:49,311
Ready.

832
00:28:50,103 --> 00:28:51,271
Ready, go.

833
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:54,274
One. Bring it in right away.

834
00:28:54,316 --> 00:28:55,317
Two. Right away!

835
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:56,318
Three.

836
00:28:56,526 --> 00:28:57,527
Four.

837
00:28:57,611 --> 00:28:58,528
Five.

838
00:28:58,612 --> 00:29:00,906
A NICE FINISH

839
00:29:00,989 --> 00:29:02,324
PATRICIA IS NEXT
Hit the buzzer.

840
00:29:02,366 --> 00:29:04,117
Now, shuffle back and forth.

841
00:29:06,078 --> 00:29:09,206
Could you call it out in Korean?

842
00:29:09,289 --> 00:29:10,582
"Forward!"

843
00:29:10,666 --> 00:29:11,625
THE MOST RANDOM REQUEST

844
00:29:11,667 --> 00:29:12,876
All right, sure.

845
00:29:13,168 --> 00:29:15,087
- That's a first from a foreigner, right?
- Well, yes.

846
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:16,129
Thank you.

847
00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:17,923
Let's move back and forth.

848
00:29:18,548 --> 00:29:20,259
One.

849
00:29:20,342 --> 00:29:21,843
Shuffle back and forth.

850
00:29:21,927 --> 00:29:22,844
One-two.

851
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:24,346
Good.

852
00:29:24,388 --> 00:29:25,264
She's strong.

853
00:29:25,681 --> 00:29:26,682
One.

854
00:29:28,141 --> 00:29:29,142
One-two.

855
00:29:30,143 --> 00:29:32,020
When you move forward... Let's pause.

856
00:29:32,062 --> 00:29:33,522
- Your torso is leaning forward.
- Yes.

857
00:29:33,605 --> 00:29:36,400
Don't lose your balance.
Move your whole body forward together.

858
00:29:36,483 --> 00:29:37,651
WITH RENEWED DETERMINATION

859
00:29:37,693 --> 00:29:38,527
One.

860
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:40,237
FIST FORWARD, FOOT BACKWARD

861
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:42,489
My coordination is awful.

862
00:29:42,531 --> 00:29:43,532
It can be very tricky.

863
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:45,242
Viewers might find...

864
00:29:45,325 --> 00:29:48,370
Trust me, I'm not messing around.

865
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:51,206
It's really challenging.
You must be exhausted.

866
00:29:51,290 --> 00:29:52,582
You're like an animated emoji.

867
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:54,042
So cute.

868
00:29:54,126 --> 00:29:55,627
One.

869
00:29:55,711 --> 00:29:56,586
One-two.

870
00:29:59,673 --> 00:30:01,341
One more time. One-two.

871
00:30:01,383 --> 00:30:02,592
- Nice job.
- One-two.

872
00:30:02,676 --> 00:30:05,721
Same as Wonhee,
wrap it up with five one-two combos.

873
00:30:05,762 --> 00:30:07,264
- Okay.
- Keep calling it out in Korean?

874
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:08,223
Yes.

875
00:30:08,307 --> 00:30:10,851
- I'll keep giving orders in Korean.
- Got it.

876
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:12,102
You've got this. Ready.

877
00:30:12,185 --> 00:30:13,228
I can do this!

878
00:30:13,270 --> 00:30:14,396
Ready, go.

879
00:30:14,730 --> 00:30:16,189
- One-two.
- One.

880
00:30:16,231 --> 00:30:17,733
- One-two. Step back.
- Two.

881
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:19,359
- One-two. Step back.
- Three.

882
00:30:19,401 --> 00:30:20,402
One-two.

883
00:30:21,862 --> 00:30:22,988
Oh, no.

884
00:30:23,071 --> 00:30:24,656
Maybe it was too much for you.

885
00:30:24,740 --> 00:30:26,783
<i>This is so embarrassing!</i>

886
00:30:26,867 --> 00:30:29,578
<i>- Don't say that.</i>
<i>- Not at all. You just did your best.</i>

887
00:30:29,870 --> 00:30:33,415
Why don't you rest a bit on the side?

888
00:30:33,457 --> 00:30:35,625
- Can I?
- You can observe for now.

889
00:30:35,709 --> 00:30:36,585
Okay.

890
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:38,545
Watch and learn from the side.

891
00:30:38,587 --> 00:30:39,921
All right, Wonhee.

892
00:30:40,005 --> 00:30:42,758
- You'll learn how to throw a hook.
- Okay.

893
00:30:42,799 --> 00:30:45,594
Think of it as a circular punch thrown
while staying balanced.

894
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:47,596
Aim for your opponent's temple.

895
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:50,098
Oh, no. I wanted to learn this one.

896
00:30:50,140 --> 00:30:53,518
I have a target at home!

897
00:30:53,602 --> 00:30:55,312
I'll show you the basic stance.

898
00:30:57,522 --> 00:31:00,067
Take this stance. Look.

899
00:31:02,194 --> 00:31:03,612
Turn with the second punch.

900
00:31:03,695 --> 00:31:05,322
There you go. From that position,

901
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:08,283
swing your arm in an arc.

902
00:31:08,325 --> 00:31:09,659
- "Shut it!"
- That's it.

903
00:31:09,743 --> 00:31:11,870
That was great. Turn.

904
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,955
From that position,

905
00:31:14,289 --> 00:31:15,457
swing your right hand, too.

906
00:31:15,499 --> 00:31:16,333
Exactly.

907
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:17,959
That was good, but one thing.

908
00:31:18,043 --> 00:31:20,128
Your torso is leaning forward.

909
00:31:20,170 --> 00:31:22,547
Keep your balance while punching.

910
00:31:22,631 --> 00:31:24,341
- Let's give it a go.
- Okay.

911
00:31:25,759 --> 00:31:26,760
Double hook.

912
00:31:27,928 --> 00:31:29,346
Double hook.

913
00:31:29,846 --> 00:31:31,098
- Double hook.
- Double hook. Good.

914
00:31:31,139 --> 00:31:32,641
- What do I do with my legs?
- You should

915
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:34,351
turn your back foot on "two."

916
00:31:35,394 --> 00:31:36,228
Exactly.

917
00:31:36,311 --> 00:31:38,480
Just like that, turn your left foot.

918
00:31:38,814 --> 00:31:39,689
- Double...
- Right.

919
00:31:39,773 --> 00:31:41,525
FOOTWORK MATCHES THE FISTS
Turn your right foot.

920
00:31:41,817 --> 00:31:43,985
- Double hook.
- There you go.

921
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:45,320
- Just...
- Double hook.

922
00:31:45,821 --> 00:31:47,447
- She's so cute.
- It's...

923
00:31:47,489 --> 00:31:49,324
From where I'm looking,

924
00:31:49,366 --> 00:31:51,159
- you look like a dancing penguin.
- Right.

925
00:31:51,201 --> 00:31:53,120
THIS PENGUIN CAN BOX NOW

926
00:31:53,161 --> 00:31:53,995
That's it.

927
00:31:54,079 --> 00:31:55,997
- She just nailed it.
- Yes, totally.

928
00:31:56,039 --> 00:31:58,250
Try again. Ready, go.

929
00:31:58,917 --> 00:31:59,751
Double hook.

930
00:31:59,835 --> 00:32:01,503
PERFECT FOOTWORK
Nicely done.

931
00:32:01,545 --> 00:32:03,839
Let me check your progress with mitt work.

932
00:32:03,880 --> 00:32:05,424
Let's step this way.

933
00:32:05,507 --> 00:32:06,842
MORE SERIOUS NOW

934
00:32:06,883 --> 00:32:07,759
Ready, go.

935
00:32:08,677 --> 00:32:10,554
Double hook. You're doing so well.

936
00:32:10,637 --> 00:32:12,764
- One more time.
- She's talented.

937
00:32:13,515 --> 00:32:16,309
Double hook. Okay, that was nice.

938
00:32:16,351 --> 00:32:17,686
RAW TALENT DISCOVERED
She's a natural.

939
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:19,813
I should stay put.

940
00:32:19,855 --> 00:32:22,774
Let's wrap this up with ten sets
of one-two combo and double hook.

941
00:32:22,858 --> 00:32:24,317
One-two, double hook.

942
00:32:24,359 --> 00:32:25,360
Let's go.

943
00:32:25,402 --> 00:32:27,112
- One-two, double hook.
- One-two, double hook.

944
00:32:27,195 --> 00:32:28,196
She's good.

945
00:32:28,280 --> 00:32:29,531
One-two, double hook.

946
00:32:29,614 --> 00:32:31,241
Okay. Good job. One more time.

947
00:32:31,324 --> 00:32:32,492
One-two, double hook.

948
00:32:32,534 --> 00:32:33,618
Three. One more time.

949
00:32:33,702 --> 00:32:35,036
One-two, double hook.

950
00:32:35,078 --> 00:32:36,121
Five. Hey!

951
00:32:37,539 --> 00:32:38,498
One last time!

952
00:32:39,416 --> 00:32:41,376
CHARISMATIC FINISH
Thank you, Wonhee.

953
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:43,837
- You're great.
- Totally.

954
00:32:43,879 --> 00:32:45,464
You're really good at this.

955
00:32:45,547 --> 00:32:46,465
MUFFLED APPLAUSE

956
00:32:46,548 --> 00:32:49,009
Jabs feel a little playful

957
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:51,052
because they go like this.

958
00:32:51,094 --> 00:32:52,554
But hooks make you look cool.

959
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:54,473
- It has big movements.
- You're right.

960
00:32:54,556 --> 00:32:56,391
You're right. In an actual match,

961
00:32:56,433 --> 00:32:59,561
when a hook hits you
right in the jaw or the temple...

962
00:32:59,644 --> 00:33:00,479
You go down?

963
00:33:00,562 --> 00:33:02,063
- Yes, you do.
- Really?

964
00:33:02,147 --> 00:33:03,315
How bad is the injury?

965
00:33:03,398 --> 00:33:04,566
I'd like to use it on my brother.

966
00:33:05,233 --> 00:33:07,360
If you're using it on Jonathan...

967
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,862
I'd like to know the recovery window.

968
00:33:08,904 --> 00:33:11,114
I'll tell you something more useful.

969
00:33:11,198 --> 00:33:12,616
Throw a straight.

970
00:33:12,699 --> 00:33:14,701
It's the punch you throw
as you twist your back foot.

971
00:33:14,743 --> 00:33:16,495
- Like this?
- Add hooks, too.

972
00:33:16,578 --> 00:33:18,747
A straight and a double hook.
Then he'll go down.

973
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:20,874
THANKS FOR THE GREAT TIP

974
00:33:20,916 --> 00:33:22,209
- There you go.
- That's nice.

975
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:24,711
- I'll have to ask him to stand still.
- All right.

976
00:33:24,753 --> 00:33:26,755
Now that you learned how to throw punches,

977
00:33:26,796 --> 00:33:28,507
- let's go on to sparring.
- What?

978
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:31,426
Sparring? I'm so jealous.

979
00:33:31,468 --> 00:33:33,011
Sparring? Who's my partner?

980
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:36,765
COACH JA-DOO VS WONHEE

981
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:38,475
Get in the ring, Wonhee.

982
00:33:38,558 --> 00:33:39,392
FIGHTER ENTERS

983
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:44,606
ROOKIE BOXER
WONHEE

984
00:33:47,859 --> 00:33:48,777
Oh, shoot.

985
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:50,779
You're making me anxious. Take it easy.

986
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:53,114
RIZZ OVERLOAD

987
00:33:53,156 --> 00:33:55,116
Coach me from the sidelines, Patricia.

988
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:56,535
ONE-DAY COACH
PATRICIA

989
00:33:56,618 --> 00:33:58,036
Hey, Coach. What should I do?

990
00:33:58,119 --> 00:34:00,038
- You're going to win.
- Really?

991
00:34:00,121 --> 00:34:01,998
- What do I do when I'm cornered?
- With your hooks...

992
00:34:02,082 --> 00:34:03,792
- When you're cornered?
- How do I escape?

993
00:34:03,833 --> 00:34:04,918
Just drop to the floor.

994
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,336
- Sink to the floor?
- That's it.

995
00:34:06,419 --> 00:34:07,504
I'm going to do that.

996
00:34:08,630 --> 00:34:10,131
- Or try acting cute.
- Randomly,

997
00:34:10,215 --> 00:34:11,800
"Hey, that hurts."

998
00:34:11,883 --> 00:34:13,510
- "It hurts."
- But keep this in mind.

999
00:34:13,593 --> 00:34:15,303
- We're not backing down.
- That's right.

1000
00:34:15,387 --> 00:34:17,639
Don't go easy on him
just because he taught you the moves.

1001
00:34:17,722 --> 00:34:20,600
First off, I'll go over the rules.

1002
00:34:20,642 --> 00:34:24,020
Anywhere above the belt line is fair game.

1003
00:34:24,104 --> 00:34:26,106
The same goes for both sides.

1004
00:34:26,147 --> 00:34:29,818
But you can't hit your opponent
behind the neck or on the back.

1005
00:34:29,901 --> 00:34:32,487
When you hit, use your knuckles.

1006
00:34:32,571 --> 00:34:36,992
- The flat side here?
- Yes, you can only strike with that side.

1007
00:34:37,033 --> 00:34:38,451
- I'll use my left hand only.
- Okay.

1008
00:34:38,493 --> 00:34:39,327
GIVING WONHEE A HANDICAP

1009
00:34:39,411 --> 00:34:40,787
How long is a round?

1010
00:34:40,829 --> 00:34:43,540
A round usually lasts 3 minutes,
but ours will be 2 minutes.

1011
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:45,834
Let's give it a go.

1012
00:34:45,875 --> 00:34:47,669
All right. Begin!

1013
00:34:48,003 --> 00:34:49,671
PRE-FIGHT BOW
Let's give it a go.

1014
00:34:49,754 --> 00:34:51,089
Glove touch.

1015
00:34:52,257 --> 00:34:53,800
Go ahead and hit me.

1016
00:34:53,842 --> 00:34:54,676
Hit me.

1017
00:34:54,759 --> 00:34:56,636
Good. There you go.

1018
00:34:56,678 --> 00:34:57,846
SWIFT PUNCHES

1019
00:34:57,929 --> 00:34:59,389
Hey, you're doing great.

1020
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:01,975
You're doing great, Wonhee.

1021
00:35:02,017 --> 00:35:05,312
PAYBACK FOR THE WORKOUTS

1022
00:35:05,353 --> 00:35:07,731
REVENGE-FUELED JABS
Let's go, Wonhee!

1023
00:35:07,814 --> 00:35:09,858
FLUSTERED
Wow, you're really doing great.

1024
00:35:11,359 --> 00:35:12,777
UNEXPECTED JABS

1025
00:35:12,861 --> 00:35:13,945
Great job.

1026
00:35:14,029 --> 00:35:14,863
BACKS AWAY

1027
00:35:14,904 --> 00:35:16,197
Take a breather!

1028
00:35:16,239 --> 00:35:18,700
A SUDDEN WWE MOVE?

1029
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:20,201
ONE-DAY COACH LOVES JABS

1030
00:35:22,495 --> 00:35:25,290
A SUDDEN HOOK

1031
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:27,208
You're brilliant, Wonhee.

1032
00:35:27,250 --> 00:35:29,711
- He's going too easy on me.
- Not at all.

1033
00:35:29,753 --> 00:35:30,879
I'm fighting back.

1034
00:35:31,755 --> 00:35:32,797
What happened?

1035
00:35:32,881 --> 00:35:33,882
MOMMY!

1036
00:35:33,923 --> 00:35:36,801
Sorry, it's all for the show.

1037
00:35:36,885 --> 00:35:38,386
- Don't worry.
- It's purely for the show.

1038
00:35:38,428 --> 00:35:39,429
COACH CHOI GETS SHOWBIZ

1039
00:35:39,512 --> 00:35:41,222
There he goes.

1040
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:43,850
Feel free to hit me.
I'll defend this time.

1041
00:35:44,059 --> 00:35:45,518
You can't, though.

1042
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:46,811
Stay on offense.

1043
00:35:47,771 --> 00:35:49,731
RUTHLESS ATTACKER

1044
00:35:50,398 --> 00:35:51,524
You're doing great.

1045
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:52,567
What's going on?

1046
00:35:52,609 --> 00:35:53,985
GUINEA PIG RUNS AWAY

1047
00:35:54,069 --> 00:35:55,362
Wonhee, you poor thing.

1048
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:56,237
I'm exhausted.

1049
00:35:56,321 --> 00:35:57,864
- Come on.
- Wait.

1050
00:35:57,906 --> 00:35:59,074
- It's over.
- No.

1051
00:35:59,115 --> 00:36:01,242
- That bell means 30 seconds left.
- What? Oh, no.

1052
00:36:03,036 --> 00:36:04,287
Do I guard like this?

1053
00:36:04,371 --> 00:36:05,372
Yes, hold both arms like this.

1054
00:36:05,413 --> 00:36:06,956
Put up a guard like this.

1055
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:07,874
Try blocking.

1056
00:36:08,083 --> 00:36:09,250
- There you go.
- I've got this.

1057
00:36:09,334 --> 00:36:12,087
What kind of opponent is that nice?

1058
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:13,672
PULL IT TOGETHER, COACH

1059
00:36:15,382 --> 00:36:17,008
ROUND 1 OF THE SLUGFEST ENDS

1060
00:36:17,384 --> 00:36:19,427
You're great, Wonhee.

1061
00:36:19,552 --> 00:36:20,845
Just a second.

1062
00:36:20,929 --> 00:36:23,431
DOWN TO 30% HP

1063
00:36:23,473 --> 00:36:25,225
She's got a talent.

1064
00:36:25,266 --> 00:36:27,394
- She's very quick on the attack.
- Right?

1065
00:36:27,435 --> 00:36:28,812
MY GIRL HAS SKILLS

1066
00:36:28,895 --> 00:36:30,647
At the start...

1067
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:32,273
SHORTEST 1 MINUTE BREAK EVER

1068
00:36:32,315 --> 00:36:33,650
- What was that?
- On your feet.

1069
00:36:33,733 --> 00:36:35,026
- That went by so fast.
- Come on.

1070
00:36:35,110 --> 00:36:36,486
- You've got this!
- Get up.

1071
00:36:36,569 --> 00:36:37,779
BUT I WANT TO REST

1072
00:36:37,862 --> 00:36:40,782
Jab with your left,
then throw a right straight.

1073
00:36:40,824 --> 00:36:42,283
A jab with my left.

1074
00:36:42,367 --> 00:36:45,120
A right straight.
That's it. You get it now.

1075
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:46,830
She's picking it up so fast.

1076
00:36:47,622 --> 00:36:49,582
DEFENSE WORK REVIEW COMPLETE

1077
00:36:49,624 --> 00:36:50,875
All right, Wonhee.

1078
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:52,460
You're on fire!

1079
00:36:52,544 --> 00:36:53,878
Just a bit more!

1080
00:36:56,131 --> 00:36:57,340
Now, give him a roundhouse kick!

1081
00:36:57,424 --> 00:36:58,299
Wait, wrong sport.

1082
00:36:58,341 --> 00:36:59,467
Wait, stop.

1083
00:37:00,135 --> 00:37:01,261
You can't do that.

1084
00:37:01,302 --> 00:37:03,138
My bad.

1085
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:05,473
- Attack!
- Reach a bit further.

1086
00:37:05,515 --> 00:37:06,349
Hang on.

1087
00:37:06,433 --> 00:37:08,351
Our girl is drained.

1088
00:37:08,810 --> 00:37:10,562
- Go, Wonhee!
- Take deep breaths.

1089
00:37:11,187 --> 00:37:12,272
- Okay.
- You're doing great.

1090
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:14,691
Give me all you've got
at the 30-second warning.

1091
00:37:14,774 --> 00:37:16,735
You're up for it, aren't you?

1092
00:37:16,818 --> 00:37:19,028
I'VE TRAINED FOR THIS MOMENT

1093
00:37:19,696 --> 00:37:21,406
SHE ENDURED BRUTAL TRAINING

1094
00:37:21,489 --> 00:37:22,991
TO LEAVE NO REGRETS

1095
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:28,121
SHE'LL LEAVE IT ALL IN THE RING

1096
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:30,165
SHE WON'T LET HER SUPPORTERS DOWN
We have chocolate milk.

1097
00:37:30,790 --> 00:37:32,125
Ready.

1098
00:37:32,167 --> 00:37:33,501
Final 30 seconds.

1099
00:37:33,585 --> 00:37:34,878
- Here we go.
- Let's go!

1100
00:37:35,336 --> 00:37:36,421
You're doing amazing.

1101
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:39,841
Give me four punches.

1102
00:37:39,883 --> 00:37:41,676
PUSHING HARDER THAN EVER

1103
00:37:41,885 --> 00:37:42,844
Go for his side!

1104
00:37:42,886 --> 00:37:44,971
WONHEE ON OFFENSE

1105
00:37:47,390 --> 00:37:48,933
Go harder. You've got this!

1106
00:37:49,100 --> 00:37:50,393
10 SECONDS LEFT
You're almost there.

1107
00:37:50,477 --> 00:37:54,189
DRAWING ON EVERY LAST OUNCE
OF HER STRENGTH

1108
00:37:54,230 --> 00:37:56,608
That last move was fire. Kudos, Wonhee.

1109
00:37:57,150 --> 00:37:59,652
PUSHING HERSELF TO THE LIMIT

1110
00:37:59,861 --> 00:38:01,529
ROUND 2 ENDS

1111
00:38:01,696 --> 00:38:03,448
Glove touch.

1112
00:38:03,782 --> 00:38:05,950
SPARRING ENDS

1113
00:38:06,034 --> 00:38:07,702
TOWELS ARE READY
Come here, Wonhee.

1114
00:38:10,371 --> 00:38:12,207
Well done. Be proud of yourself.

1115
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:13,458
Good work.

1116
00:38:13,541 --> 00:38:15,126
She's got it.

1117
00:38:15,210 --> 00:38:17,378
Coach Choi was going easy on me,
but I couldn't keep up.

1118
00:38:17,462 --> 00:38:19,339
Sparring for two rounds is no joke.

1119
00:38:19,380 --> 00:38:22,342
You might think, "Why is she so weak?"

1120
00:38:22,383 --> 00:38:24,135
But it's really exhausting.

1121
00:38:24,219 --> 00:38:26,137
I would drop to the floor and give up.

1122
00:38:26,221 --> 00:38:30,099
Amateur boxers fight
two two-minute rounds.

1123
00:38:30,183 --> 00:38:31,559
You're at that level.

1124
00:38:31,643 --> 00:38:32,644
A SEAL OF APPROVAL

1125
00:38:32,727 --> 00:38:33,978
Your punches are great, too.

1126
00:38:34,062 --> 00:38:35,355
- So...
- Thank you.

1127
00:38:35,396 --> 00:38:36,940
That concludes our mini game.

1128
00:38:37,023 --> 00:38:38,650
Tell us the winner.

1129
00:38:38,733 --> 00:38:39,776
The winner is...

1130
00:38:40,276 --> 00:38:42,111
Wonhee!

1131
00:38:42,195 --> 00:38:43,404
Congrats.

1132
00:38:43,446 --> 00:38:45,240
- Thank you.
- All right, Wonhee!

1133
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:46,449
- Thank you.
- You're amazing!

1134
00:38:46,533 --> 00:38:47,575
Coach!

1135
00:38:47,617 --> 00:38:50,829
I SHARE THIS HONOR WITH MY COACH

1136
00:38:51,955 --> 00:38:53,540
Gosh, she's so cool.

1137
00:38:53,581 --> 00:38:55,625
Why am I the one sweating?

1138
00:38:55,708 --> 00:38:57,544
Thank you for training us.

1139
00:38:57,585 --> 00:38:58,962
BOWS TO COACH CHOI

1140
00:38:59,045 --> 00:39:00,922
Thank you, Coach.

1141
00:39:01,005 --> 00:39:03,216
- Thank you, guys.
- I'm out of here.

1142
00:39:06,094 --> 00:39:07,929
TRAINING ENDS

1143
00:39:07,971 --> 00:39:09,973
What did you think about boxing?

1144
00:39:10,265 --> 00:39:11,516
ESPECIALLY DEEP SIGH

1145
00:39:11,599 --> 00:39:12,934
My eyes are tearing up.

1146
00:39:14,310 --> 00:39:15,603
Such a shame, right?

1147
00:39:15,645 --> 00:39:17,272
I had so much fun.

1148
00:39:17,355 --> 00:39:19,399
But I've always wanted to go on the ring.

1149
00:39:19,941 --> 00:39:20,859
You know what?

1150
00:39:20,942 --> 00:39:22,068
I think I'm cut out for this.

1151
00:39:22,110 --> 00:39:23,611
- I felt that, too.
- I had fun.

1152
00:39:23,653 --> 00:39:24,863
Coach Choi felt it, too.

1153
00:39:24,946 --> 00:39:27,365
- He could sense your talent.
- Because of my strength?

1154
00:39:27,448 --> 00:39:29,409
- He said you were on another level.
- Really?

1155
00:39:29,450 --> 00:39:31,536
- I could've been his star student.
- What a shame.

1156
00:39:31,619 --> 00:39:33,121
How was it for you?

1157
00:39:33,204 --> 00:39:36,249
I realized it's much harder
than I expected.

1158
00:39:36,624 --> 00:39:38,960
You did great for your first time.

1159
00:39:39,002 --> 00:39:40,420
We both did great.

1160
00:39:40,461 --> 00:39:42,505
- I think we make a great duo.
- You know what?

1161
00:39:42,589 --> 00:39:44,465
Maybe we should keep training here.

1162
00:39:44,549 --> 00:39:45,758
We can stay here.

1163
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:47,135
- We'll take over.
- Like tyrants.

1164
00:39:47,218 --> 00:39:48,928
We can stay back.

1165
00:39:48,970 --> 00:39:50,054
<i>We can keep training.</i>

1166
00:39:50,138 --> 00:39:50,972
THE GIRLIES' BOXING GYM

1167
00:39:51,014 --> 00:39:55,351
Do you always spread
this much positive energy around?

1168
00:39:55,435 --> 00:39:58,396
- I think I am. I like that.
- That's so nice.

1169
00:39:58,479 --> 00:39:59,814
I like making others laugh.

1170
00:39:59,856 --> 00:40:03,484
It makes me happy
when people laugh at my jokes.

1171
00:40:03,526 --> 00:40:05,987
It makes me more talkative.
I guess I'm an attention seeker.

1172
00:40:06,029 --> 00:40:07,155
Am I using that right?

1173
00:40:07,238 --> 00:40:10,116
If I had to train alone with Coach Choi,
it would've been awkward.

1174
00:40:10,491 --> 00:40:11,826
Really?

1175
00:40:12,660 --> 00:40:14,662
- I'm shy around new people.
- You are?

1176
00:40:14,746 --> 00:40:16,831
Thanks to your energy,

1177
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:18,958
- I had it so easy. I'm so grateful.
- Really?

1178
00:40:19,292 --> 00:40:21,252
- I'm glad to hear that.
- I can't thank you enough.

1179
00:40:21,336 --> 00:40:26,716
Still, you can't be full of energy
all the time.

1180
00:40:26,799 --> 00:40:29,093
When do I feel tired?

1181
00:40:29,177 --> 00:40:30,762
When the food coma hits.

1182
00:40:31,346 --> 00:40:33,014
Food coma is no joke.

1183
00:40:33,056 --> 00:40:36,643
My favorite thing is
eating well and taking a nap.

1184
00:40:36,684 --> 00:40:39,896
People think something's wrong with me
when I'm really just full.

1185
00:40:39,979 --> 00:40:41,606
How cute is that?

1186
00:40:41,689 --> 00:40:47,070
I can't really think of times
when I feel down.

1187
00:40:47,153 --> 00:40:49,447
Maybe you're just naturally cheerful.

1188
00:40:49,530 --> 00:40:51,282
You're like the sun.

1189
00:40:51,366 --> 00:40:53,034
- I'm very energetic.
- You're like a ray of sunshine.

1190
00:40:53,076 --> 00:40:54,285
A ray of sunshine?

1191
00:40:54,369 --> 00:40:55,787
You're like a ray of sunshine.

1192
00:40:55,870 --> 00:40:56,871
That's a good one.

1193
00:40:56,955 --> 00:40:57,997
MS. SUNSHINE

1194
00:40:58,039 --> 00:41:01,042
What's your secret to staying so positive?

1195
00:41:01,084 --> 00:41:02,710
Positive thinking.

1196
00:41:02,794 --> 00:41:04,712
- You make an effort to think that way.
- Yes, I do.

1197
00:41:04,796 --> 00:41:06,214
Are you seeing anyone?

1198
00:41:06,255 --> 00:41:07,423
No.

1199
00:41:07,507 --> 00:41:09,300
I'm not in a relationship.

1200
00:41:09,384 --> 00:41:12,553
I heard you once tried to ask out
Jonathan's friend.

1201
00:41:12,595 --> 00:41:14,597
- About that.
- Can I ask about it?

1202
00:41:14,681 --> 00:41:16,891
I talk about that story everywhere I go.

1203
00:41:16,933 --> 00:41:19,560
At this point,
I should print the story on a T-shirt.

1204
00:41:19,602 --> 00:41:21,688
I'll tell you how it happened.
When I was little,

1205
00:41:21,729 --> 00:41:23,064
I had a crush on this boy.

1206
00:41:23,147 --> 00:41:25,066
- And he was Jonathan's friend?
- Yes.

1207
00:41:25,149 --> 00:41:26,025
Oh, my.

1208
00:41:26,067 --> 00:41:27,360
Here's what happened.

1209
00:41:27,402 --> 00:41:29,779
I told him that I liked him.

1210
00:41:30,113 --> 00:41:31,906
You won't believe what happened next.

1211
00:41:31,990 --> 00:41:33,449
He transferred schools within a week.

1212
00:41:33,992 --> 00:41:35,451
I drove him away.

1213
00:41:35,535 --> 00:41:36,911
But that's not on you.

1214
00:41:36,953 --> 00:41:38,329
Right?

1215
00:41:38,413 --> 00:41:39,580
But Jonathan kept telling me

1216
00:41:39,622 --> 00:41:41,916
- how I was responsible for that.
- That's so mean.

1217
00:41:41,958 --> 00:41:43,376
There were about four of them.

1218
00:41:43,418 --> 00:41:44,585
I drove them all away.

1219
00:41:44,669 --> 00:41:46,587
- So there were multiple guys?
- Yes.

1220
00:41:46,629 --> 00:41:49,716
TOO MANY COINCIDENCES
He calls me a repeat offender.

1221
00:41:49,757 --> 00:41:52,468
Since that's the case,
it's easier to misunderstand,

1222
00:41:52,552 --> 00:41:55,096
but you couldn't have been
the deciding factor.

1223
00:41:55,138 --> 00:41:57,223
Their family finances or other issues
must've been involved,

1224
00:41:57,265 --> 00:41:58,599
not some schoolgirl's confession.

1225
00:41:58,683 --> 00:42:00,518
- Right? So--
- That can't have done it.

1226
00:42:00,601 --> 00:42:03,730
- None of it was on me.
- Of course not. Don't you worry.

1227
00:42:03,771 --> 00:42:05,481
Why are you comforting me?

1228
00:42:06,107 --> 00:42:09,068
Because Jonathan keeps blaming you.

1229
00:42:09,110 --> 00:42:10,069
I can relate.

1230
00:42:10,111 --> 00:42:12,113
I hear Jonathan keeps an eye
on your male friends.

1231
00:42:12,196 --> 00:42:13,698
I'm really curious, though.

1232
00:42:13,781 --> 00:42:15,158
- Mine doesn't.
- Is he the weird one?

1233
00:42:15,241 --> 00:42:17,076
- He is.
- Really?

1234
00:42:17,118 --> 00:42:19,037
Let's say I go out.

1235
00:42:19,120 --> 00:42:21,247
When he asks who I'm with,
I have to tell him.

1236
00:42:21,289 --> 00:42:22,498
Wait, I get it now.

1237
00:42:22,582 --> 00:42:24,167
You were never the reason.

1238
00:42:24,250 --> 00:42:29,130
Maybe Jonathan scared off
the guys you liked.

1239
00:42:29,172 --> 00:42:30,423
That's not it.

1240
00:42:30,465 --> 00:42:32,008
He keeps nagging

1241
00:42:32,091 --> 00:42:34,010
because he doesn't want
to lose his friends.

1242
00:42:34,093 --> 00:42:36,637
He's keeping an eye on me
so he won't lose more friends.

1243
00:42:36,679 --> 00:42:39,640
Do you get it now?
I didn't want to spell that out myself.

1244
00:42:39,724 --> 00:42:41,267
But that's the truth.

1245
00:42:41,309 --> 00:42:42,477
JONATHAN HAD HIS REASONS

1246
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:45,813
That's so petty, though.
What's wrong with him?

1247
00:42:45,855 --> 00:42:47,648
You're really good at this.

1248
00:42:47,732 --> 00:42:49,650
Are you flirting with me?

1249
00:42:49,734 --> 00:42:51,110
Sure.

1250
00:42:51,152 --> 00:42:53,738
THAT WORKED

1251
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:56,657
I saw your potential as a boxer today.

1252
00:42:56,741 --> 00:42:58,659
Are there any other sports
you'd like to try?

1253
00:42:58,701 --> 00:43:02,371
Boxing was something
I'd always wanted to try.

1254
00:43:02,455 --> 00:43:03,748
What was this called again?

1255
00:43:03,831 --> 00:43:04,957
- Climbing?
- Yes, climbing.

1256
00:43:06,334 --> 00:43:08,002
- I'm also interested.
- You are?

1257
00:43:08,086 --> 00:43:09,212
I want to try it,

1258
00:43:09,295 --> 00:43:11,255
but it scares me.

1259
00:43:11,631 --> 00:43:12,840
- In case you might fall?
- Yeah.

1260
00:43:12,882 --> 00:43:14,175
I have another favorite.

1261
00:43:14,342 --> 00:43:16,677
- Swimming. I love the water.
- Oh, really?

1262
00:43:16,761 --> 00:43:18,888
- Me too.
- I can't wait to go swimming again.

1263
00:43:18,971 --> 00:43:22,767
I sometimes book a hotel
just to use their swimming pool.

1264
00:43:22,850 --> 00:43:24,310
- Honestly--
- I can't swim, though.

1265
00:43:24,352 --> 00:43:27,939
Even after my debut, I went
to a community sports center for a swim.

1266
00:43:28,022 --> 00:43:29,857
I even wore fins.

1267
00:43:29,941 --> 00:43:30,900
You must be pretty good.

1268
00:43:30,983 --> 00:43:32,151
LIKE A MERMAID

1269
00:43:32,193 --> 00:43:34,612
All I can manage is this
while standing in the pool.

1270
00:43:34,695 --> 00:43:36,197
Basically, I just walk around.

1271
00:43:36,239 --> 00:43:37,365
JUST WALKING AROUND

1272
00:43:37,406 --> 00:43:39,325
I'd love to go swimming with you.

1273
00:43:39,367 --> 00:43:40,243
We're a match.

1274
00:43:40,326 --> 00:43:41,285
HERE'S MY WORKOUT BUDDY

1275
00:43:41,369 --> 00:43:44,831
I always ask this question
to all the guests on my show.

1276
00:43:45,206 --> 00:43:47,291
Do you have any advice for me
as I navigate my 20th year?

1277
00:43:47,375 --> 00:43:49,752
Experience as many different things
as you can.

1278
00:43:49,836 --> 00:43:51,295
Even small things.

1279
00:43:51,379 --> 00:43:53,923
- Like traveling alone?
- Or going to a café alone.

1280
00:43:54,006 --> 00:43:56,342
- I've never been to a café alone.
- Right?

1281
00:43:56,384 --> 00:43:58,511
You'll find a lot of things
you haven't tried before.

1282
00:43:58,553 --> 00:44:00,555
When I was 20...

1283
00:44:00,596 --> 00:44:01,514
Well...

1284
00:44:01,556 --> 00:44:02,932
I was busy working.

1285
00:44:03,015 --> 00:44:05,726
While I appreciated
all the opportunities I was given,

1286
00:44:05,768 --> 00:44:07,228
it kept me from trying new things.

1287
00:44:07,270 --> 00:44:09,397
You mostly gained
work-related experiences.

1288
00:44:09,438 --> 00:44:11,399
I never got to travel alone.

1289
00:44:11,440 --> 00:44:12,984
I can't even eat out alone.

1290
00:44:13,067 --> 00:44:14,068
- Even now?
- Yes.

1291
00:44:14,152 --> 00:44:16,320
- I've never tried it before.
- Really?

1292
00:44:16,404 --> 00:44:18,030
You'll be surprised to hear my list.

1293
00:44:18,072 --> 00:44:19,407
I've never traveled alone.

1294
00:44:19,448 --> 00:44:21,576
Some people go on solo trips, right?

1295
00:44:21,617 --> 00:44:25,538
- Hanging out with friends?
- Yes, I never got to experience that.

1296
00:44:25,580 --> 00:44:30,001
I think it's really important
to make time for yourself.

1297
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:31,961
Just try things head-on.

1298
00:44:32,044 --> 00:44:33,421
- "Head-on"?
- Yeah.

1299
00:44:33,504 --> 00:44:36,132
I get very anxious about failure.

1300
00:44:36,215 --> 00:44:38,092
- Me too.
- It frightens me so much

1301
00:44:38,134 --> 00:44:40,469
that I always hesitate
before starting something new.

1302
00:44:41,137 --> 00:44:42,930
- Same.
- I see. So...

1303
00:44:43,222 --> 00:44:44,849
I'm still struggling with this,

1304
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:47,476
but I think it's a good challenge
for people in their 20s.

1305
00:44:47,560 --> 00:44:51,314
I know it sounds odd, but you're
at a good age to learn to accept failures.

1306
00:44:51,522 --> 00:44:56,444
I believe failures build resiliency

1307
00:44:56,527 --> 00:44:58,905
and allow you to become stronger.

1308
00:44:58,946 --> 00:45:01,657
That's what I want to tell you.
I never got to do that.

1309
00:45:01,741 --> 00:45:02,742
BE STRONG, WONHEE

1310
00:45:02,783 --> 00:45:05,036
- That's so wise.
- I never got to do that.

1311
00:45:05,912 --> 00:45:07,997
Thank you for your amazing advice.

1312
00:45:08,080 --> 00:45:09,081
- Let's meet again--
- Huh?

1313
00:45:09,123 --> 00:45:10,833
- That's it for the day?
- Yes.

1314
00:45:10,917 --> 00:45:13,294
- Thank you for your kind words.
- Was that an interview?

1315
00:45:13,336 --> 00:45:15,296
Yes, thanks for your wisdom.

1316
00:45:15,338 --> 00:45:18,424
- No problem.
- Let's try a new sport next time.

1317
00:45:18,466 --> 00:45:19,926
I'd love that. Next time,

1318
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:22,094
we can try swimming
and other sports together.

1319
00:45:22,303 --> 00:45:24,472
Thank you.

1320
00:45:24,639 --> 00:45:26,182
<i>My gosh, Wonhee.</i>

1321
00:45:26,265 --> 00:45:29,477
"DON'T BE AFRAID OF FAILURES
AND FACE CHALLENGES HEAD-ON"

